WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.010
- Oh my gosh, you're funny!

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:02.850
So, I'm leading with that.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:03.683
Have you met Jay before?

00:00:03.683 --> 00:00:05.460
- No, I'm like sandwiched,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.430
in between like two
American icons right now.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.530
- I love that I'm somehow
in the same sentence as him,

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.997
thank you.

00:00:11.997 --> 00:00:14.460
- Is that the old Mr. Beef restaurant?

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.720
- It is.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.867
- That's my favorite. My
picture is on the wall.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:18.965
- Yes. Your picture is on the wall.

00:00:18.965 --> 00:00:21.420
- That is the most guy-centric restaurant.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.580
There's not a vegetable
in a hundred miles.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.413
- [Ayo] No, no.

00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:27.210
- It's just like a sausage rolled

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.650
Italian beef in a roll.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.656
They dip the whole thing
in some kind of grease.

00:00:30.656 --> 00:00:32.085
Fantastic!

00:00:32.085 --> 00:00:33.784
(audience laughs)

00:00:33.784 --> 00:00:35.085
- My mouth just watered
and I'm not a dude.

00:00:35.085 --> 00:00:36.960
I think it sounds awesome.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.090
I heard that you wanted
to ask Jay something.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:39.923
- Well, I mean,

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.110
it's sort of, we could
discuss it, you know.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.080
I don't know if there's
like an overt question.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.656
- Oh, okay.

00:00:47.656 --> 00:00:50.370
- I did, I got my license for the show.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.560
I'm from the East Coast and so I-

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.393
- Where did you grow up?

00:00:53.393 --> 00:00:54.301
- I grew up in Boston.

00:00:54.301 --> 00:00:55.140
- Oh! I'm in Boston! Where in Boston?

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.370
- I'm from Dorchester.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.200
- Are you a double-decker
or a triple-decker?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.033
- Triple-decker.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:00:59.970
- Ooh, ooh!

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.432
- [Kelly-] Alright, alright, alright.

00:01:01.432 --> 00:01:03.543
- Oh, I'm sorry. Triple-decker, yeah.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.120
Now, those are all the cool houses.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:06.953
- [Ayo] Yeah.

00:01:06.953 --> 00:01:08.010
- So you didn't drive there?

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.000
- I didn't drive there.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.740
I just took the T and
then I went to school

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.992
in New York, and I was like,

00:01:11.992 --> 00:01:13.350
"I'm gonna take the train forever.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.430
I'm gonna live forever".

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:16.552
And then I moved out here, and I was like,

00:01:16.552 --> 00:01:17.385
"What are we doing? We're driving?"

00:01:17.385 --> 00:01:19.560
- See, that's my nightmare:
taking the train forever.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.270
- An adult skill that I needed to have?

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.980
- Do you find...do you like it?

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.200
Are you comfortable doing it or no?

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.886
- When you drive...

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.010
- Yeah, I like driving.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.030
It's me imagining driving,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:30.913
No, I like it.

00:01:30.913 --> 00:01:34.980
I like putting on a song,
I've never driven before.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:35.813
- [Kelly] Yeah! A playlist!

00:01:35.813 --> 00:01:37.816
- I like putting like
a playlist, you know,

00:01:37.816 --> 00:01:38.649
kinda like getting in a zone.

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:41.190
- You'll get to know
this is your alone time.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.023
- Yes.

00:01:42.023 --> 00:01:43.050
- I like alone time.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:45.318
- Yeah, don't get in
a zone. Drive the car.

00:01:45.318 --> 00:01:47.430
(hosts and audience laugh)

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.610
- Yeah, don't go in a zone.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:51.600
- Okay. So you started out
learning comedy in Boston,

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.440
like Jay, right?

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.273
- Yeah.

00:01:53.273 --> 00:01:54.690
- What was that like?

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.176
- It was a lot of open mic nights

00:01:57.176 --> 00:02:01.147
and my friends and I, we
were kind of interested.

00:02:01.147 --> 00:02:02.850
I feel like we got
interested pretty young.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.160
And so it was like, us in high school,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.347
like a bunch of weirdos who
did improv and were like

00:02:08.347 --> 00:02:09.616
"We could try this stand up thing".

00:02:09.616 --> 00:02:10.470
(audience coos)

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.303
- [Ayo] Yes.

00:02:11.303 --> 00:02:12.602
- [Kelly] I think that's so cool.

00:02:12.602 --> 00:02:14.910
- So that very strange person

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.370
going to like, an open mic night in Boston

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.500
where it's like, all
these, you know, like,

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.360
dudes, especially.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.193
- Grown people.

00:02:22.193 --> 00:02:24.420
- Who are like, "Ugh! Let
me tell you about my wife".

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:25.426
And I'm like-

00:02:25.426 --> 00:02:26.610
(audience laughs)

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.290
- But Boston's a great comedy town

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.163
cause it's such a quirky, odd place.

00:02:31.163 --> 00:02:32.010
- [Ayo] Yeah.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:32.843
- I love Boston.

00:02:32.843 --> 00:02:34.664
It's one of my favorite touring stops.

00:02:34.664 --> 00:02:35.497
- Oh!

00:02:35.497 --> 00:02:38.964
- Here's a, I'm gonna give
you a Boston compliment.

00:02:38.964 --> 00:02:41.180
(Jay fumbles for words)

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.151
I'll try to use different words.

00:02:44.151 --> 00:02:44.984
(Ayo chuckles)

00:02:44.984 --> 00:02:46.050
Guy says to me, "Hey, my friend!"

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:46.987
This stranger,

00:02:46.987 --> 00:02:48.382
"My friend met you in California.

00:02:48.382 --> 00:02:50.430
He said, You're not an (muted)".

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.263
- Yep.

00:02:51.263 --> 00:02:52.500
- I went, "Oh, well thanks."

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.601
The guy goes, "No, really!"

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:55.980
I go, "Well, thank you very much, sir.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:56.820
I appreciate that".

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.702
And that, I mean, that's
a compliment in Boston!

00:02:58.702 --> 00:03:01.470
- When the show came out,

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:05.833
my parents came to the
premiere, and my dad was like,

00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:08.610
"You know, I think I'll
actually watch this one".

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.730
And I was like, "Oh! Thanks dad".

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.273
An he was like, "No,
no! Really! I mean it!"

00:03:13.273 --> 00:03:14.129
- Yeah! Exactly!

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:17.187
- "Really! I'm gonna watch it!"

00:03:17.187 --> 00:03:18.020
And he did.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.025
- And it's very suspicious in Boston,

00:03:19.025 --> 00:03:20.940
"What are you, in California now?

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.070
You got a gardener out there?

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.340
Or you do your own gardening?"

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.276
I do my own garden.

00:03:24.276 --> 00:03:25.433
"Oh, okay."

00:03:25.433 --> 00:03:27.360
(audience laughs)

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:28.650
- They're like sizing you.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.130
- You can't be putting on those airs.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:32.553
- You know, triple-decker accredited all.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.370
That's a whole other level.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:37.770
- Well, I wanna say congrats on The Bear.

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:38.760
I mean, so much success.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.350
For those of you who haven't seen it,

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:41.569
tell everybody what is it about.

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:44.299
- It is about a restaurant in Chicago.

00:03:44.299 --> 00:03:46.410
It's an Italian beef restaurant

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.859
and just the people who work there,

00:03:48.859 --> 00:03:52.380
when they get along, when
they don't, and yeah.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.530
Just trying to make it like a legit place.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.630
- Yeah. It's amazing. It did so well.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.118
Everybody was talking about it all summer.

00:03:59.118 --> 00:03:59.951
- Oh yeah. It's a lot of fun.

00:03:59.951 --> 00:04:01.230
And it's a real place.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:02.958
- Whenever I'm in Chicago, I go there-

00:04:02.958 --> 00:04:05.310
- Your picture. I'm, like,

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.377
I've looked at your picture
while we were filming.

00:04:07.377 --> 00:04:08.347
It's on the wall.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:09.603
- I'm like 19 in that picture. Yeah.

00:04:09.603 --> 00:04:12.097
And it looks all, it's all cleaned up.

00:04:12.097 --> 00:04:14.490
Oh, there it is! There you go, Mr. Beef!

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.630
That's hilarious.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.784
- I love the name of this place. Right?

00:04:17.784 --> 00:04:18.750
(audience laughs)

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:19.800
You're walking around.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.202
I'm a little hungry. Mr. Beef!

00:04:21.202 --> 00:04:23.520
- You know you're not
getting a veggie burger

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:24.446
when you go in.

00:04:24.446 --> 00:04:27.006
- Mr. Beef. Every
vegetarian is going in, yes.

00:04:27.006 --> 00:04:30.217
- It's like stepping in
a time capsule there too.

00:04:30.217 --> 00:04:33.815
It's like, they're Cash
Only still I think.

00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:36.660
It's like, everybody who works there

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:37.737
has worked there for forever.

00:04:37.737 --> 00:04:40.200
They're like all such a family.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:41.430
- I Love those kind of places.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.867
- Yeah. It's really cool.

00:04:42.867 --> 00:04:44.598
- Well, this is a good segway.

00:04:44.598 --> 00:04:47.880
We will all be doing some
cooking in our next segment.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.004
You look scared.

00:04:49.004 --> 00:04:51.546
- I got a heads up about the recipe.

00:04:51.546 --> 00:04:53.080
I got a heads up.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.560
- Okay. The Bear is streaming now on Hulu.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.793
You've got to watch it.

